==Latin==

===Etymology===
From {{der|la|ine-pro|*tóm}}, accusative of {{m|ine-pro|*só}}. Confer with its feminine form {{cog|la|tam}}, as in {{m|la|cum}}-{{m|la|quam}}, {{m|la|num}}-{{m|la|nam}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|Classical}} {{IPA|/tum/|lang=la}}
* {{audio|la-cls-tum.ogg|Audio (Classical)|lang=la}}

===Adverb===
{{la-adv|tum||-}}

# [[then]], [[thereupon]]
#: '''''Tum''' Caecilius in horto sedet.'' - ''Then Caecilius sits in the garden.''
# [[at the time]], at that time, then
#* {{Q|la|Livy|Ab Urbe Condita|26|1|quote=Ea '''tum''' cura maxime intentos habebat Romanos, non ab ira tantum, quae in nullam unquam ciuitatem iustior fuit, quam quod urbs tam nobilis ac potens, sicut defectione sua traxerat aliquot populos, ita recepta inclinatura rursus animos uidebatur ad ueteris imperii respectum.|year=27-25 BCE|trans=This concern in particular troubled the mindful Romans '''at the time''', not so much because of anger, which has never been more justified against any other city, rather because a city so noble and powerful, in the same way that it had attracted the support of a number of communities by its revolt, was thought would again turn attention back towards respect for the previous government once recaptured.}}
# [[further]] [[on]]
#: ''...'''tum''' silvis scaena coruscis...'' - Aeneid, Book 1, Line 164

